0..75 Comment "//! `halted` holds an open access across an operation with no continuation."
76..79 Comment "//!"
80..159 Comment "//! An overflow must stop the computation. The cleanup of each open access must"
160..204 Comment "//! still run, as it runs after `abandon k`."
205..208 Comment "//!"
209..284 Comment "//! A clause of such an operation abandons the continuation, then gives its"
285..362 Comment "//! body. So the cleanup of the access runs, as it runs where a clause writes"
363..426 Comment "//! `abandon k` itself. Each pair of examples gives one answer."
427..430 Comment "//!"
431..485 Comment "//! - see: #7968 — an operation with no continuation"
486..546 Comment "//! - see: `unwound.gandr` — the cleanup after `abandon k`"
